1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Finding a trading setup doesn’t have to start with hours of searching.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,200
Once you have the Options Traders Academy OS, save it directly to your phone or computer as a shortcut

3
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:17,100
so your trading system is always one click away.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,000
Log into your OTA OS and start inside your profile.

5
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:26,600
From there, open Your Daily Play.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,400
This is where you begin building your strategy.

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:39,200
Enter the ticker you want to analyze and choose whether you’re looking for an options setup or a futures setup.

8
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:43,300
You decide what market you want to study.

9
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:46,300
The OS helps you organize the analysis.

10
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:50,300
Next, pull your charts from TradingView.

11
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:57,300
Upload your full intraday view, four-hour, one-hour, fifteen-minute, and five-minute charts.

12
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:02,000
Those timeframes give the system the market structure it needs.

13
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:08,500
Once your charts are uploaded, OTA OS analyzes the information and builds your plan.

14
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:16,200
It may identify a bullish setup, a bearish setup — or tell you there’s no trade worth taking yet.

15
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:20,200
Then read the full strategy.

16
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:28,000
The system helps you identify the directional bias, important levels, confirmation, possible entry conditions, exits, and risk considerations.

17
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:33,500
And when the better decision may simply be to sit on your hands.

18
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:41,900
For options setups, continue through the analysis and review the contract or strike the system identifies.

19
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,800
Then open your brokerage platform — we use Robinhood —

20
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:49,700
find that contract, and add it to your watchlist.

21
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:57,700
And this part matters: a contract appearing on your screen does not mean you automatically buy it.

22
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:03,600
Watch the setup. Confirm the conditions. Review the contract yourself. Manage your risk.

23
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,100
Then decide whether the opportunity fits your trading plan.

24
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:17,500
That’s how you use the Options Traders Academy OS to go from a ticker, to market analysis, to a structured trading plan.

25
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,200
No technology can predict what the market will do next.

26
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:32,000
The advantage is having a system that helps you analyze the information, organize the setup, and make a more informed decision instead of guessing.

27
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,800
Because trading isn’t about trying to catch every move.

28
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:44,800
It’s about having a strategy, waiting for confirmation, managing your risk, and using technology to build a stronger edge.

